---
title: Homemade Custard
servings: 6-8
source: https://youtu.be/OtVD5DYwHC8
tags:
  - dessert
  - custard
  - vanilla
  - sauce
---

-- ============================================================
-- VANILLA & MILK INFUSION
-- ============================================================

Split the @vanilla bean{1} lengthways with the tip of a #knife{}, then lay it on its back and run the knife along the pod to scrape out the seeds.

Pour the @milk{500%ml} and @single cream{550%ml} [- source says 500-600 ml; midpoint used -] into a #saucepan{} over medium-high heat. Add the vanilla seeds and the scraped pod (or keep the pod aside to make vanilla sugar in a jar of sugar instead). Bring up to a simmer, then let it simmer for ~infusion{5%minutes} to draw out the vanilla flavour.

-- ============================================================
-- EGG MIXTURE
-- ============================================================

Meanwhile, in a #large bowl{}, whisk the @egg yolks{8} with @sugar{60%g} [- source: 5 tbsp, converted at ~12.5 g/tbsp -] using a #whisk{} until pale and silky.

Whisk in @corn flour{1%tsp} until there are no lumps. -- Only needed with single cream; with double cream it can be skipped as it's already thick enough.

-- ============================================================
-- COMBINING & COOKING
-- ============================================================

Temper the eggs: whisk a splash of the hot milk mixture into the egg yolks so the eggs aren't shocked. Once combined, pour the egg mixture back into the #saucepan{} with the rest of the milk and cream (removing the vanilla pod first if you like).

Cook over a low heat, stirring in figures of eight so it heats evenly and gently, for ~{3%minutes} [- source: 2-4 minutes -], until thickened.

Check it's ready by dipping a #spoon{} in the custard and running a finger through the coating on the back -- if the line holds and doesn't run, the custard is done. Serve hot.
